{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1123290-help-me-write-a-campaign-about-the-technocracy-s-collapse","id":1123290,"title":"Help me write a campaign about the Technocracy's collapse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-31T20:21:09-07:00","id":1123290,"title":"Help me write a campaign about the Technocracy's collapse","content":"I've done many Technocracy games in the past but one of the things I've always done is depict the Technocracy as a group which was never as stable or powerful as it thought it was. Indeed, I've had a more Soviet Union meets the Illuminati feel for it than anything else. Going with the idea that militant totalitarian groups need a enemy, I have the idea the Technocracy finally collapsed in 2017 due to the fact it hadn't been at war with the Traditions for a decade.<br /> <br /> My idea is it has broken up into multiple competing and even Civil War prone factions.<br /> <br /> The Throne: An homage to the Seers of the Throne, the Throne is a faction of the Technocracy which has abandoned any and all pretense of being out for humanity and wish to use their powers to be as rich and powerful as possible. The Throne is allied with Pentex and the Camarilla's equivalent in my games and basically offer a very simple ultimatum to mages they encounter. &quot;Do you want be rich or dead?&quot; They may be allied with Threat: Null but primarily preserve Consensual Reality not to promote humanity but to make sure they're the only people with magick. The Throne actively works to slow down human progress and kill advancements that would lead to people awakening as they want to be the only people with that power. Their response to this treason to anything the Union stands for? &quot;Oh, grow up.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Thrones, notably, have added a NWO religion methodology which is effectively converted Celestial Choir, Akashic Brotherhood, and other Traditionalists who work to promote fundamentalist anti-science religious practices. It is a godless organization which truly offends many of its Traditionalist counterparts but wields great power in places the Union used to be quite weak.<br /> <br /> The Nationalists: Technocrats who have decided to infiltrate themselves into the governments of their home nations and work on a local level. The United States, Russian Federation, European Union, People's Republic of China, and so on are all separate factions now. This has also made them very very powerful within their spheres but they now work against each other. They've created several false organizations to work out of like Valkyrie, Majestic-12, Rainbow, and a newer bigger SAD.<br /> <br /> The Nationalists in America have accidentally clued way too many members of the establishment onto the supernatural and are presently scrambling to make up for that.<br /> <br /> Invictus: The reformer element of the Union has joined itself with the Sons of Courage to become basically Technocrat Monster Hunters. They've opted out of the Technocracy's Civil War (as this is generally called). Instead, Invictus works to hunt vampires, Revenants, Nephandi, and other creatures which go bump in the night. Invictus is growing because it's allied with Hunters and many Traditionalist mages have actually been willing to lend assistance. Invictus is probably more educated about supernaturals than most Technocrats now but is caught between the choice of whether to go after all reality-deviants or just the &quot;bad&quot; ones. There's more than cynicism at work there since they don't have the resources for the former.<br /> <br /> It has very high casualties but more or less equality between Acolytes and Enlightened Personnel.<br /> <br /> The Foundation: An alliance of Iteration X, Progenitors, Void Engineers, and Syndicate mages which have a much simpler goal than most. They exist for the purposes of advancing human science and technology, screw the whole reality war thing (which they are massively hypocritical on). The Syndicate mages here generally serve as marketeers while the bulk of the power is with the scientists and engineers. It's extremely rich and controls numerous former companies. Oddly, the Foundation does keep its own army and actively hates the Traditions. Generally, though, they prefer to fight the Ascension War with words and money. They are also at war as much with the Throne as anyone else.<br /> <br /> The Foundation has notably a loose alliance with the Virtual Adepts and has been working with them to try to &quot;convert&quot; the Sons of Ether into a group which would follow a coherent technocratic paradigm. There's been a big huge fight in the latter in my games anyway between the consistent scientists (essentially Technocrats allied to the Traditions who want a looser but not ridiculous paradigm) and the pseudo-science nutters.<br /> <br /> Esoterrorists: More of a catch-all term for Technocrats who have started flooding the markets of the supernatural world with Technocracy equipment. Part of this is ideological as they take a weird Reverse-Taftani approach to Consensual Reality as arming people with laser guns, robots, nanotechnology, and so on will improve the Union's paradigm as long as some of it work. They also protect themselves by leaving Paradox and the effects to fall on the people they sell them to. Other parts are for money or revenge.<br /> <br /> I'm debating going with different factions than these and am open to suggestions. I also would love to hear how people would think this might affect the setting, Traditions, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:24:58-07:00","id":1123317,"title":"","content":"I like the Esoterrorists. They should be putting out a lot of <i>Terminator</i> robots since that franchise has legs and be behind many glitzy sci-fi movies. . . <br /> <br /> As for the Foundation, I'd say they have a tough job getting the Etherites into a larger Technocratic group. The Etherites were burned pretty back by the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> What role do you see the players taking in this Technocracy Civil War?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}